  "notes": [
   "The award is a Certificate of Competency (#36743) leading to a high school diploma; the catalog counts it in high school credits ('Students will complete a total of 160 high school credits'; 'A minimum of 20 residency credits must be completed at Mt. San Antonio College'), not units or hours. total_units left null because the stated total is in high school credits, a different measure; measure set to 'units' by default since no hours are printed.",
   "The Units column of the course table is blank for every course, so all course units are null.",
   "All courses are printed under 'Required Courses' with no selection rule, so the block is recorded as 'all'. In practice the list (including overlapping math paths such as Algebra 1/2 and Integrated Math 1-3, and Pre-Algebra, ELD, Study Skills) likely functions as a menu toward 160 credits; a reviewer should verify the actual graduation requirements.",
   "BSHS SPNS1 and BSHS SPNS2 are printed as 'or' options to BSHS SPN1 and BSHS SPN2 and are recorded as alternatives.",
